  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q25-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "25",
    "prompt": "Find the coefficient of $x^3$ in the expansion of $(x+2)^2(x+1)^4$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$44$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x+2)^2&=x^2+4x+4\\\\(x+1)^4&=x^4+4x^3+6x^2+4x+1\\end{align*}$$\nThe matching products that give $x^3$ are $x^2(4x)$, $4x(6x^2)$ and $4(4x^3)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Coefficient of }x^3&=1\\times4+4\\times6+4\\times4\\\\\\text{Coefficient of }x^3&=44\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
